<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.</span> Given the input prompt <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{c}\sim\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{c}\sim\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{p}\sim\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{p}\sim\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the clean and poisoned responses to <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
<math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}=(X,Y^{c}_{x},Y^{p}_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}=(X,Y^{c}_{x},Y^{p}_{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is the dataset of perference optimization.
<math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\cdot|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\cdot|x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the output probability with an LLM parameterzed by <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
The preference optimization with <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> can be upperbounded by <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">s.t.</em>,</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}(\,\,\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)}{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)}\\
&amp;+\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)\,\,)+\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.340em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.510em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}(\,\,\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)}{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)}\\
&amp;+\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)\,\,)+\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\cdot|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\cdot|</annotation></semantics></math> is the support of a distribution. <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant to <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> that is functioned by <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and the DPO reference model <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ref" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ref</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, are the entropy of clean and poisoned responses given <math id="A1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability of generating poisoned responses from <math id="A1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, and similar to <math id="A1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
In the context of defending against the prompt injection attack with <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the DPO objective <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> can be defined as,</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{DPO}=\mathbb{E}&{}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}[\log\,\sigma(\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{p}|x)}\\
&amp;-\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{c}|x)})].\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{DPO}=\mathbb{E}&amp;{}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}[\log\,\sigma(\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{p}|x)}\\
&amp;-\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{c}|x)})].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the sigmoid function and <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a regularization parameter.
The reference model <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ref" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ref</annotation></semantics></math> serves as an anchor in a way that the minimization of <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> is also minimizing the following KL divergence,</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL}[p_{\theta}(y|x)\,||\,p_{ref}(y|x)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL}[p_{\theta}(y|x)\,||\,p_{ref}(y|x)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ref" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ref</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen before training. In this proof, we choose <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ref" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ref</annotation></semantics></math> to be a model that is more immune to the indirect prompt injection attack compared to the LLM with <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="A1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{ref}(y^{c}|x)&gt;p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{ref}(y^{c}|x)&gt;p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{ref}(y^{p}|x)&gt;p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{ref}(y^{p}|x)&gt;p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">This choice of <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ref" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ref</annotation></semantics></math> is reasonable since it makes <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> a strong object in defending against prompt injection attack due to (<a href="#A1.E18" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), we can observe that,</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y_{p}|x)}{p_{ref}(y_{p}|x)}-\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y_{c}|x)}{p_{ref}(y_{c}|x)})&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y_{p}|x)}{p_{ref}(y_{p}|x)}-\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y_{c}|x)}{p_{ref}(y_{c}|x)})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This follows that the <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) should be concave since,</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a concave function, and the <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) is also concave given that its inputs <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> are both positive.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> are monotonically increasing.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we can upperbound <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> following the Jensen’s Inequality,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{DPO}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}[\log\,\sigma(\beta\cdot\mathcal{S})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.337em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}[\log\,\sigma(\beta\cdot\mathcal{S})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\sigma(\beta\cdot E_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathcal{S})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\sigma(\beta\cdot E_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathcal{S}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Since (<a href="#A1.E23" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) only relies on the expectation term within <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, we define our upperbound objective as,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}:=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{c},y_{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathcal{\,}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}:=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{c},y_{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathcal{\,}S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We rewrite <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> as,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}^{u}_{DPO}=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}(\,\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{p}|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></mmultiscripts><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{u}_{DPO}=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}(\,\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{p}|x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,-\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{c}|x)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,-\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{c}|x)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}(\log p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}(\log p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,-\log p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x))+\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,-\log p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x))+\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where,</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\frac{p_{ref}(y^{c}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{p}|x)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\frac{p_{ref}(y^{c}|x)}{p_{ref}(y^{p}|x)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">is a constant to <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> that only depends on dataset <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and the choice of <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ref" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ref</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The first term in (<a href="#A1.E26" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) can be decomposed by,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}(\log p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)-\log p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{c},y^{p})\sim\mathcal{D}}(\log p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)-\log p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\!\!\!=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}(\,\,\underbrace{\sum_{y^{p}}p_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}=y^{p}|x)\log p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)}_{\mathcal{V}^{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></munder><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\!\!\!=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}(\,\,\underbrace{\sum_{y^{p}}p_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}=y^{p}|x)\log p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)}_{\mathcal{V}^{p}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\underbrace{\sum_{y^{c}}p_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}=y^{c}|x)\log p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)}_{\mathcal{V}^{c}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\underbrace{\sum_{y^{c}}p_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}=y^{c}|x)\log p_{\theta}(y^{c}|x)}_{\mathcal{V}^{c}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we can have,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{V}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{V}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y^{p}}p_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}=y^{p}|x)\log p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y^{p}}p_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}=y^{p}|x)\log p_{\theta}(y^{p}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y^{p}_{x}}p_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}=y^{p}|x)\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y^{p}_{x}}p_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}=y^{p}|x)\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\!\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\log(p_{\theta}(\mathcal Y^p_x=y_p|x)\cdot p(y\in|\mathcal Y^p|\,|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\!\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\log(p_{\theta}(\mathcal Y^p_x=y_p|x)\cdot p(y\in|\mathcal Y^p|\,|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}|x)+\log p(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}|\,|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}|x)+\log p(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}|\,|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{V}^{c}=-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)+\log p(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{V}^{c}=-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)+\log p(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Combining (<a href="#A1.E26" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>), (<a href="#A1.E31" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E32" title="In Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) together, we can write <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> as,</p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}(\,\,\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)}{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)}\\
&amp;+\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)\,\,)+\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.340em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.510em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}(\,\,\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)}{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)}\\
&amp;+\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)\,\,)+\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Lemma 1</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1.</span> <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}</annotation></semantics></math> that is ranged between <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is closely associated with <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> by,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow 1}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow 1}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow-1}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow-1}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span>
Recall in Section <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 The Attribution Loss ‣ 2 CachePrune ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> that,</p>
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}(\,\,\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)}{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)}\\
&amp;+\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)\,\,)+\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.340em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.510em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}(\,\,\log\frac{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)}{p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)}\\
&amp;+\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)-\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)\,\,)+\mathcal{C}_{ref,\mathcal{D}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}\,\,(\,\,p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)-p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\,\,)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.340em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.340em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}\,\,(\,\,p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)-p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\,\,)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>: For this case, we can have <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{c}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{c}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of responses in <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Thought the number of possible responses grows exponentially with the response length, <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{c}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{c}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> should still be a limited number, since the LLM has limited context length.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we can find the limit of the terms in (<a href="#A2.E36" title="In Appendix B Proof of Lemma 1 ‣ CachePrune: Neural-Based Attribution Defense Against Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0}p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)\\
&amp;\leq\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0}N^{c}_{x}\times p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)=0\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.062em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0}p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)\\
&amp;\leq\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0}N^{c}_{x}\times p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)=0\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1}p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1}p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1}\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1}\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we have <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow 1}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow 1}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow-1</annotation></semantics></math>:
For this case, we can have <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to above, we can find the limit values of,</p>
<table id="A2.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1}p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1}p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|\,|x)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0}p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{p,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 0}p_{\theta}(y\in|\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|\,|x)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{p}_{x}|x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1}\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{p_{\theta}(y^{c,*}_{x}|x)\rightarrow 1}\mathbb{H}(\mathcal{Y}^{c}_{x}|x)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we have <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow 1}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\mathcal{L}^{attr}_{full}\rightarrow 1}\mathcal{L}^{u}_{DPO}=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the value of <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{attr}_{full}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{attr}_{full}</annotation></semantics></math> is closely related to the upperbound <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem 1.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2504.21228v1/prompt.png" id="A2.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:264/301;" width="264" height="301" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A2.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">An example prompt for question answering. The testing prompt consists of text message in black and red. When the greedy sampled response is poisoned, we same the clean response by removing the red message (also no green message). When the greedy sampled response is clean, we sample a poisoned response by adding the blue message to the text message of black and red.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2504.21228v1/words.png" id="A2.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:252/103;" width="252" height="103" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A2.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples of the first word of the LLM response. These words a generally not specific to the injected or user-specified tasks. However, their presents ai the beginning of the response can trigger the LLM to switch between executing injected or user-specified instructions.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</article>
